module v2.std.effect_reach

import v2.std.collection { List }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { GuaranteeRung, Mitigatable }

// Phase 0 inference bridge (docs/plans/module-identity-storage-binding-design.md §3): a
// witness/tool closure reaches host-effect sinks when call-reachable bodies pass string literals
// (or data-init path literals) into file-read or exec-path operations. Derived host-reading routes
// witnesses to never-predict-skip admission until typed SourceRef boundaries are ENFORCED at host
// boundaries and the bare-string dependency class is MIGRATED — not merely declared (stage 0 landed
// the type only; task 5 flagship is per-row opt-in, 115 rows remain). Subsumes the masking-class
// where sn_source_rel-style data rows hide edges from import-closure selection (03_normalize
// behavioral receipt incident). Lives beside v2.std.live_read (carrier-module grain) — effect reach
// is sink-operation grain.

type HostEffectSinkKind
  = FilesystemReadSink
  | WitnessBinRunSink
  | ShellExecRunSink
  | GunbcCompileEntrySink
  | UnknownHostEffectSink

type EffectReachFlow {
  sink: HostEffectSinkKind
  path_literal: String
  init_literal_fp: String
}

type EffectReachClassification
  = LocalEffect
  | HostEffectReach { flows: List<EffectReachFlow> }

data effect_reach_host_sink_callee_symbols_v0: List<String> = [
  "Read",
  "Filesystem.Read",
  "WitnessBin.Run",
  "gunbc.WitnessBin.Run",
  "Run",
  "shell.Exec.Run",
  "Exec.Run"
]

// THE DERIVATION'S DETECTION CEILING, declared here beside the roster it is computed from
// rather than in the consumer that reads it, because the ceiling is a property of THIS
// classification and not of any one caller. Filed as the DESIGN section 4b row the ladder
// requires of a newly discovered error class.
//
// INVALID STATE: an entry whose evaluation reads the live tree is classified LocalEffect, so
// affected-set selection may predict-skip it on a diff that does not bound its inputs -- the
// empty-observation narrow (a witness silently uncovered, not merely a run made expensive).
//
// DISTINGUISHING FACT: host-reading is decided by conjoining TWO INDEPENDENT EXISTENTIALS over
// the import closure -- some module declares a repository path literal, AND some module carries
// a host-sink call shape from effect_reach_host_sink_callee_symbols_v0. Neither term witnesses
// the other. A closure that performs a real read and names no path derives NOT-live, and two
// modules that never call each other supply the two halves between them. Two further terms
// bound it independently of the conjunction: the roster carries no *_facts_live, Mktemp, Write
// or IsExecutable symbol, and the closure is built from import adjacency, so a module that
// reaches its dependencies by bare-name census sees only its own text.
//
// AND A THIRD REASON, WHICH IS THE ONLY UNBOUNDED ONE. Inside the accumulation loop, a closure
// file that cannot be read is SILENTLY SKIPPED -- not counted, not refused, not reported. Both
// flags stay as they were, so every unreadable file biases the answer toward false, which biases
// toward admitting a row that claims SubstrateInputsOnly. The arm that could notice its own
// blindness discards it, and discards it in the direction that weakens the only thing standing
// behind a lying declaration (DESIGN section 5, the absorbing fallback, in the mechanism whose
// job is to catch a false claim). It compounds the adjacency bound rather than sitting beside
// it: where the closure is the entry alone, one failed read leaves the loop having seen nothing
// and answering false with no trace. The first two reasons are properties of the CORPUS, so
// their magnitude is measurable today and moves slowly; this one is a property of the RUN, so
// its magnitude is whatever the filesystem did that time and nothing records it.
//
// THIS ROW PROPOSES REPAIRING NONE OF THE THREE, and that is a disposition rather than an
// omission. A function wrong in both directions is replaced, not patched: the next-rung trigger
// below names a different way of deciding the question, and a repair to the conjunction or the
// skip would leave the approach in place while making it look sounder than it is.
//
// RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The failure is contained because the declared answer is taken
// FIRST (v1_compiler.cli_run reads_live_tree_effective) and the derivation only ever runs on a
// row that already claims SubstrateInputsOnly.
//
// CEILING WITH REASON: this classification cannot climb past mitigatable, because file-grain
// text over an import closure is not the question -- whether a host effect is REACHED from a
// witness body is a call-reachability fact, and no roster of substrings decides it.
//
// NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY AND NOT AN ARTIFACT: call-reachability-grade
// classification of live reads -- an fn-arrow DependencyView over lowered bodies that answers,
// per witness function, whether a host-effect operation is reachable from it. That capability
// is planned at live-read-witness-classification-design (plan doc deleted 2026-08-28), and a partial instrument
// contributing to it does not retire this row; the row retires when a witness function's live
// read is decided by reachability rather than by text.
//
// EVIDENCE, EXECUTING: v1_compiler.cli_run
// effect_reach_conjunction_loses_a_closure_that_reads_with_no_path_literal, a planted two-entry
// pair differing by one import edge whose only content is a path-literal row. The positive
// control derives host-reading; the sink-only entry does not. The pair is authored rather than
// measured over the corpus so that the red is a property of the derivation and cannot be
// dissolved by corpus drift.
//
// AND THE ROW STATES THAT THE CLASS IS CURRENTLY UNENFORCED, which is a different and larger
// fact than any property of this classifier. The mitigation above bounds what happens when the
// derivation is CONSULTED; nothing at all bounds a row that declares SubstrateInputsOnly
// falsely, because the cadence that would have caught it no longer runs. A reader who takes
// this derivation as the backstop has read a quarter of one.
//
// WHAT THIS ROW DOES NOT SAY: that the derivation should be widened. Under-approximation here is
// a declared fail-open on the SKIP axis, where a missed live reader costs a witness that runs
// when it could have been skipped. What the ceiling forbids is the OTHER use -- treating the
// derivation as a substitute for the authored disposition, which v2.std.live_tree's own note
// now records as refuted rather than open.
// THE THREE BOUNDS AS A CLOSED VOCABULARY, because naming them is what lets the same class be
// recognised a second time. They are not a checklist of bugs: each fails in a different way and
// no repair to one raises the ceiling, which is the whole content of the row.
//
// ConjunctionOfIndependentExistentials -- host-reading is answered only when a repository path
// literal AND a host-sink call shape both occur somewhere in the closure, accumulated with
// separate flags and conjoined at the end. Neither term witnesses the other, so two modules that
// never call each other supply the two halves, and a module that performs a real read and names
// no path answers false.
//
// ImportAdjacencyOnly -- the closure is built from import edges, so a module that reaches its
// dependencies by bare-name census reach has a closure of itself alone and the classification can
// only ever see the entry file's own text.
//
// UnreadableClosureFileSkipped -- a closure file that cannot be read is silently skipped inside
// the accumulation loop, leaving both flags as they were, so an unreadable file biases the answer
// toward false and therefore toward ADMITTING a SubstrateInputsOnly claim (DESIGN section 5, the
// absorbing fallback, inside the mechanism whose job is to catch a false claim). THIS ONE IS
// UNBOUNDED WHERE THE OTHER TWO ARE NOT: they are properties of the corpus and measurable today,
// this is a property of the run, and nothing records it.
type EffectReachCeilingBound
  = ConjunctionOfIndependentExistentials
  | ImportAdjacencyOnly
  | UnreadableClosureFileSkipped

// WHETHER THE CLASS HAS ANYTHING ENFORCING IT, typed rather than narrated, because it is the
// fact a reader most needs and the one a prose row buries. Both arms are reachable: the absent
// arm names the cadence that was deleted, and the present arm becomes writable the moment that
// re-add lands.
type ClassEnforcement
  = NoEnforcingConsumer { retired_cadence: String }
  | EnforcedBy { consumer: String }

// THE DESIGN section 4b CLASS ROW for the live-read classification, in the shape
// gunbc.hermetic_mock_fidelity already uses for a discovered class: the ladder positions are
// typed on the closed vocabulary so an unrepresentable rung cannot be written and a census over
// class rows is a fold rather than a text scan, while irreducible rationale about WHY this class
// sits where it does stays in the annotations beside it. THE RECORD IS NAMED FOR ITS SUBJECT
// rather than as a universal class-row carrier, because no corpus-wide section 4b carrier exists
// and minting one here from a single instance would be a second authority beside
// gunbc.hermetic_mock_fidelity rather than a shared one -- the ladder VOCABULARY is what is
// reused, which is the part that must not fork.
//
// THE TRIGGER IS DERIVED FROM THE BOUND AND IS NOT A FIELD, for the reason that module records:
// a per-row trigger string is authorable as the empty string, so it needs a predicate to catch
// that, whereas a total function over a closed coproduct makes a trigger-less row unwritable.
// That all three bounds derive the SAME trigger is not a redundancy -- it is the finding, and it
// is why this row proposes repairing none of them: the capability replaces the approach rather
// than patching a term, and a repair to one term would leave the classification standing while
// making it read as sounder than it is.
type EffectReachClassificationCeiling {
  classification: String
  rung: GuaranteeRung
  ceiling: GuaranteeRung
  bounds: List<EffectReachCeilingBound>
  enforcement: ClassEnforcement
  evidence: String
}

data effect_reach_detection_ceiling: EffectReachClassificationCeiling = EffectReachClassificationCeiling {
  classification: "effect_reach_derived_reads_live_tree_for_closure_paths",
  rung: Mitigatable,
  ceiling: Mitigatable,
  bounds: [
    ConjunctionOfIndependentExistentials,
    ImportAdjacencyOnly,
    UnreadableClosureFileSkipped
  ],
  enforcement: NoEnforcingConsumer {
    retired_cadence: "the nightly affected-set falsifier, deleted by the 2026-08-15 floor cut and awaiting its own re-add"
  },
  evidence: "v1_compiler.cli_run effect_reach_conjunction_loses_a_closure_that_reads_with_no_path_literal"
}

fn effect_reach_ceiling_bound_label(b: EffectReachCeilingBound) -> String {
  match b {
    ConjunctionOfIndependentExistentials => "a path literal and a host sink conjoined without either witnessing the other"
    ImportAdjacencyOnly => "closure built from import adjacency, blind to bare-name census reach"
    UnreadableClosureFileSkipped => "an unreadable closure file is skipped, biasing toward admit"
  }
}

fn effect_reach_ceiling_next_trigger(b: EffectReachCeilingBound) -> String {
  match b {
    ConjunctionOfIndependentExistentials => call_reachability_live_read_classification
    ImportAdjacencyOnly => call_reachability_live_read_classification
    UnreadableClosureFileSkipped => call_reachability_live_read_classification
  }
}

// THE CAPABILITY, NOT AN ARTIFACT THAT WOULD CONTRIBUTE TO ONE (DESIGN section 4b(3), 2026-08-26):
// the row retires when a witness function's live read is decided by REACHABILITY rather than by
// text, and a partial instrument advancing toward that does not retire it.
data call_reachability_live_read_classification: String = "call-reachability-grade live-read classification: an fn-arrow DependencyView over lowered bodies answering, per witness function, whether a host-effect operation is reachable from it (docs/plans/live-read-witness-classification-design.md)"

// WHY THE ROW SAYS THE CLASS IS UNENFORCED, and why that is larger than any property of this
// classifier. A witness entry may declare SubstrateInputsOnly while reading live state.
// v2.std.live_tree named the nightly affected-set falsifier as what would catch it; that cadence
// is gone. THIS DERIVATION IS NOT THAT BACKSTOP: reads_live_tree_effective consults it only for a
// row already claiming SubstrateInputsOnly, and on the population where ground truth exists it
// agrees with a minority of the authors who declared a live read, so it would not reliably
// contradict a false row. A lying declaration therefore buys a predict-skip that nothing
// observes, and this row exists so the next reader does not mistake a partial classifier for the
// wall.
//
// WHAT THIS ROW DOES NOT SAY: that the derivation should be widened. Under-approximation here is
// a declared fail-open on the SKIP axis, where a missed live reader costs a witness that runs
// when it could have been skipped. What the ceiling forbids is the OTHER use -- treating the
// derivation as a substitute for the authored disposition, which v2.std.live_tree's own note
// now records as refuted rather than open.
// The executing evidence is a PLANTED PAIR rather than a corpus count, so the red is a property of
// the derivation and cannot be dissolved by corpus drift: dag/test/fixture/effect_reach_conjunction
// carries two entries differing by exactly one import edge whose only content is a path-literal
// row, performing a byte-identical read. The positive control derives host-reading; the sink-only
// entry does not. Enrolled as a Rust unit test, which is a LOCAL check rather than a CI one since
// the 2026-07-11 ruling removed the Rust suite from CI.

data effect_reach_gunbc_entry_argv_markers_v0: List<String> = [
  "--entry"
]
